# Retail data (port/docs/retail-eu-plan.md, R3): the radio screen's subtitle bar with the European discs.
# SubScreenExec gives the radio screen (open_flag 0x20) an IdSub of 128 units, every other sub screen 512,
# and sets four shared id tables of ss_cmmn.dat (pesetas, main menu, etc., background) for each. The
# European tables are larger: they filled all 128 units of the radio screen and its own units, the dark
# bar behind the subtitle among them, found no room ("IDSystem::set() work full", PC runs 27.10.2026:
# IdSub 128 of 128, 46 of them main menu). Leaving the four tables out, as the European SubScreenExec
# (main.dol 0x8005a920) does, lost Hunnigan's picture (device and PC, 27.10.2026). With the European
# discs the radio screen gets the 512 units of the other screens. Nothing changes with the debug
# build's discs. A port patch for retail data.
